 think we have too  many boards and uh i think that we can  streamline that and really help  the people that are have professional  licensing  is it true that you and your family have  been subjected to death threats too in  recent days  uh yes specifically my wife has gotten  most of threats i guess they don't uh  send those directly to me but my wife  has gotten those and uh  we received we forward those on to  authorities but it's uh  very upsetting it's um it's pretty  disgusting when it's your own party  doing that  it is pretty disgusting and i'm so sorry  to hear that's happening to you and your  wife  uh you mentioned you know your own party  doing that i want to ask  we know who's doing it in terms of  sending you threats people who are angry  about the idea of donald trump losing  but who's responsible for inciting that  kind of disgusting behavior to quote  your  description well  it's people that are really spinning up  the crowd and  not even speaking truth they're not  speaking truth about the  results are not speaking truth about the  voting equipment at the end of the day  you know if i wanted to i've been in the  construction business for 40 years  i could use my what i call contractor  language and you know and scream and  holler and bellow and things like that  but i think nowadays today what we need  are people that are just going to speak  truth and and handle you know the  situation and be civil to each other  it's one thing i learned in the general  assembly i sat next to a democrat on  each side  and we would talk about bills and they  didn't maybe win me to their side and i  didn't want them to their side at least  we had conversations and i think we need  to be more civil with each other  uh not sure the president agrees on that  but it's interesting you said it's  people spinning people up against you  you didn't name the people but it's very  clear those people are donald trump  and kelly lafleur and david perdue and  other republican officials  inciting against you that's clear isn't  it  well at the end of the day i don't want  to play with people's emotions  i'm here to do a job i'm an engineer and  i just want to look at what is the  process  and where where the numbers shake out at  the end of the day and i'm going to  leave the rest  they have to you know lead their lives  and we're going around our office with  integrity  i think integrity still matters  one last question do you think if donald  trump hadn't spent much of the year  undermining mail-in voting and  dissuading his voters from mailing in  their ballots rather than staying at  home  he could have actually won a swing state  like yours fair and square  is he perhaps the author of his own  electoral demise  i believe so because the numbers show  that there were actually 24 000  republican voters that voted absentee in  the june primary  and those same 24 000 voters did not  show up to vote  in either absentee or in person on the  day of election or the 15 days of early  voting we have  so they just disappeared and they were  right for the picking they were there  in june for the primary and they should  have come home and and voted for  president trump in the fall so that's 24  000.  that's his difference right there  secretary of state brad raffensberger  thank you so much for your time  another way lindsey graham is  downplaying his  questionable behavior in georgia is by  saying  he's done the same in other states  i've talked to doug ducey in arizona  i've talked to the people in nevada  we've got contests all over the nation  the thing is arizona republican governor  doug ducey isn't in charge of elections  in that state that responsibility falls  to secretary of state katie hobbs  a democrat who said earlier today that  graham had not reached out to her  and nevada's secretary of state put out  a similar statement today  whoever graham talked to in those states  it wasn't the ultimate deciders  so for more on this arizona secretary of  state katie hobbs joins me now  thank you so much uh for coming on the  show lindsey graham says he spoke to  arizona governor doug ducey  about the vote in arizona why do you  think he didn't call you you're in  charge of that  and also what has governor duty told you  about what was said between them  well i can't begin to speculate on uh  senator graham's motives or what he  what his purpose of is in terms of  interfering in other states elections  and i have not talked to the governor  about his conversation with the senator  if lindsey graham had called you  personally to ask about non-matching  signatures on mail-in ballots for  example and the possibility  of excluding them what would you have  told him i would have told him that the  election  procedures in arizona are first of all  none of his business  and second of all that we have statutes  in place that were complied with  throughout the entire process of this  election there have been no  widespread irregularities or fraud and  claims to the contrary are just simply  false  what do you make of the fact that graham  is only making these calls to states  where trump  lost and not say north carolina where he  won a tight race  uh with a million mail-in ballots cast  funny that  well yeah it is i don't again know what  his motives are  but um i will say this again i don't  think  uh elected officials from other states  have any business  questioning the election process in in  other states  uh it's been clear throughout this  process that elected officials in our  own state don't even understand  how this works and they've all they've  done is contributed to muddying the  waters  undermining confidence in the election  and making our  jobs as election officials harder  based on what brad raffenberger says is  what lindsey graham did possibly illegal  should he have to  at least resign a senate judiciary  chairman given what he's being accused  of  well i think that is up to the senate  ethics committee  um i don't know the laws in georgia but  it sounds like  he was asking for legally cast ballots  to be thrown out  and that is highly questionable uh  behavior  and since we're talking about highly  questionable behavior rudy giuliani is  now almost all that's left of trump's  legal team in pennsylvania where he just  filed  a new brief with a court in williamsport  this comes after he humiliated himself  for four seasons total landscaping in  philadelphia  since then he's claimed the democrat  machine in philly detroit atlanta  chicago  rigged the election uh he says there's  four there's fraud by a quote foreign  company  uh pick to count the vote and that biden  supporters riot because they're lawless  all of these of course are malicious  lies i do wonder though how worried  concerned would you be  if giuliani tomorrow turns up in your  state with a bunch of new lawsuits  well again um they don't have evidence  for any of the lawsuits that have been  brought in the state of arizona  um there's two remaining challenges that  are not  uh on behalf of the trump campaign  they're on behalf of the state  republican party  um and there's really no merit to their  claims  uh so i mean i think we've seen that  they're gonna continue to throw out  these  um allegations uh until  i don't know when uh until i guess we  certify the results  uh but we are on track to certify the  state's election results on november  30th that's what we plan to do  and um you know there's really there  there's no basis for the claims that  they're making  and i i can't necessarily speak to other  states but in arizona for certain um  there there's really no legal claims  left for them to make  so just to follow up on that you know  given there's no legal basis  and given this is basically all that's  left of trump's legal  election team now a bunch of conspiracy  theorists really  uh the president has lost i think most  of the major law firms that were  representing him  do you think trump's heart is in this  legal fight or is it all just for show  well i mean we've seen the president for  months and months and months prior to  the election  already working to invalidate the  results of the election so we knew that  these kind of legal fights were coming  he's still on twitter you know making  all these false claims  um again i don't want to ascribe motives  to somebody but  he the only way he has to come out of  this  is to continue to claim that the  election was stolen  and i hope it ends soon because we are  you know  my office has been bombarded with calls  we've had to reroute calls to voicemail  so that my staff are not getting  harassed  by callers um i've been threatened my  family's been threatened  um and it would be really nice if these  uh elected leaders  would stand up and say stop the stop  the allegations our election system is  just fine here in arizona  and and and just to check uh you know  i just spoke to georgia secretary of  state who said that he's got death  threats as well did you ever think being  an election official would result in  death threats  isn't that outrageous and kind of  unprecedented  i mean i've been an elected official in  arizona for a while  uh i've seen the climate i understand  the climate  um so this is certainly not unexpected  but i do think it's uncalled for and i  think if  we didn't have elected leaders that were  fueling these conspiracies  that it would help to  tamper some of the threatening behavior  that we've seen here  and mail in voting in your state you  have a long history of mail-in voting  that all held up this time around there  were no issues  oh absolutely it worked it worked the  way it was supposed to  we saw unprecedented turnout both in  person  and in early voting by mail and we've  had a long track record of it working  well in the states so  there were no issues uh this year  katie hobbs thank you so much for your  time we'll have to leave it there
 

